      "id": "ivanhoe-source-5-p64",
      "chapterId": "ivanhoe-section-5",
      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "A traveller from the Holy Land",
      "description": "Names his calling and origin, then challenges the Templar’s own departure from Palestine. Interrupts the impending angry answer to ask how the guide knows the forest so well. Rebukes the Palmer for leaving the Holy Land and begins to answer his retort. Accompanies the travellers approaching Rotherwood as their guide identifies himself as a Palmer. Is in the approaching company when its guide declares that he is a Palmer. Travels with the retinue approaching Rotherwood while its guide names his calling.",
      "locationMarkerId": "ivanhoe-place-rotherwood-approach",
      "involvedCharacterIds": [
