      "createdAt": 1793232000000,
      "updatedAt": 1793232000000,
      "id": "ivanhoe-source-6-p18",
      "chapterId": "ivanhoe-section-6",
      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "Wilfred’s name",
      "description": "Rises with his boar-spear against the imagined insult, then mourns his estrangement from Wilfred and sits down again. Hears Cedric turn from threatening his neighbours to lamenting his absent son. Is in the household hall while Cedric’s anger gives way to regret.",
      "locationMarkerId": "ivanhoe-place-rotherwood-hall",
