      "id": "ivanhoe-source-6-p19",
      "chapterId": "ivanhoe-section-6",
      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "A horn at the gate",
      "description": "Is roused by the horn and barking and sends attendants to discover the news. Hears Cedric fear another raid while the household quiets the dogs. Waits in the hall during the interruption of Cedric’s reflection. Barks with the dogs in the hall at the horn and is among those silenced by Cedric and the domestics.",
