      "id": "ivanhoe-source-6-p21",
      "chapterId": "ivanhoe-section-6",
      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "The warder’s report",
      "description": "Returns from the gate and names the Prior and Brian de Bois-Guilbert as travellers seeking lodging. Accepts the guests and orders Hundebert to provide lodging, washing, changed clothes and supper. Hears the visitors named and Cedric’s hospitality instructions. Receives orders to take six attendants and care for the visitors and their animals. Hears the request for Norman guests to be accommodated.",
      "locationMarkerId": "ivanhoe-place-rotherwood-hall",
