      "createdAt": 1793232000000,
      "updatedAt": 1793232000000,
      "id": "ivanhoe-source-8-p45",
      "chapterId": "ivanhoe-section-8",
      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "A challenge and its pledges",
      "description": "Does not join the company’s Christian reverence to the displayed reliquary. Remains among those who do not cross themselves when the relic is produced. Names Ivanhoe as his former victor, challenges him and lays his own gold chain on the board. Guarantees Ivanhoe’s response and produces an ivory reliquary containing an alleged piece of the cross. Joins the prayers over the relic and is asked to hold the pledges. Does not join the prayers over the alleged relic of the cross; his exception is explicitly named by the narrator. Is among the company as the challenge to Ivanhoe is secured by the reliquary and gold chain.",
      "locationMarkerId": "ivanhoe-place-rotherwood-hall",
      "involvedCharacterIds": [
        "ivanhoe-character-hamet",
        "ivanhoe-character-abdalla",
        "ivanhoe-character-brian",
