      "id": "ivanhoe-source-8-p63",
      "chapterId": "ivanhoe-section-8",
      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "To the sleeping quarters",
      "description": "Is conducted to his sleeping apartment with torchbearers and refreshments. Is escorted to his assigned chamber for the night. Helps marshal the principal visitors to their sleeping rooms. Accompanies the arrangement of lodging for the travellers. Is directed toward a place of repose with the visiting retinue; the source does not identify his room. Is among the visiting retinue directed toward sleeping places; his particular room is not identified. Is directed to repose with the other visiting attendants, without a stated room or sleeping position.",
