      "id": "ivanhoe-source-9-p52",
      "chapterId": "ivanhoe-section-9",
      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "Questions at the wicket",
      "description": "Answers Wamba’s questions about prayer and penance, then calls him a Saxon fool. Waits until Gurth’s back is turned before questioning the Palmer’s influence over him and joking about Norman luck. Waits outside the postern for his mule while Wamba and the Palmer exchange their remarks.",
      "locationMarkerId": "ivanhoe-place-rotherwood-postern",
      "involvedCharacterIds": [
