      "id": "ivanhoe-source-9-p57",
      "chapterId": "ivanhoe-section-9",
      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "The narrow bridge",
      "description": "Waits with the mules on the far side of the moat and reverently kisses the Palmer’s hand. Crosses the two-plank drawbridge and mounts the borrowed mule. Crosses, secures a blue buckram bag behind his saddle and conceals it beneath his clothing. Is at the postern as the travellers mount and depart.",
      "locationMarkerId": "ivanhoe-place-rotherwood-postern-bridge",
      "involvedCharacterIds": [
