      "id": "ivanhoe-source-10-p16",
      "chapterId": "ivanhoe-section-10",
      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "A place beneath the gallery",
      "description": "Presses for a place in the foremost row for his daughter despite the Norman’s objection. Hangs on her father’s arm, frightened by the crowd’s displeasure as he tries to secure their view.",
      "locationMarkerId": "ivanhoe-place-ashby-lower-ring",
