      "createdAt": 1793232000000,
      "updatedAt": 1793232000000,
      "id": "ivanhoe-source-10-p17",
      "chapterId": "ivanhoe-section-10",
      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "The Prince arrives",
      "description": "Jostles the Norman spectator but shrinks back at the green-clad yeoman’s warning. Is still on her father’s arm below the galleries when the royal party draws the crowd’s attention. Warns Isaac against pressing his claims before attention turns to John’s entrance. Enters on a grey palfrey with a falcon and a richly dressed retinue. Rides with John in elaborate attire, unable to use his stirrups because of his boots.",
      "locationMarkerId": "ivanhoe-place-ashby-lists",
      "involvedCharacterIds": [
        "ivanhoe-character-isaac",
