      "updatedAt": 1793232000000,
      "id": "ivanhoe-source-10-p21",
      "chapterId": "ivanhoe-section-10",
      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "The gallery command",
      "description": "Answers John’s praise of Rebecca with a biblical comparison, then reminds him that she is Jewish. Orders the Saxon spectators to make room for Isaac and Rebecca. Identifies Rebecca as his daughter when John addresses them. Remains frightened by the commotion beside Isaac. Stares without moving when John orders him to yield a place. Is seated with Athelstane’s company in the gallery.",
      "locationMarkerId": "ivanhoe-place-ashby-saxon-gallery",
      "involvedCharacterIds": [
        "ivanhoe-character-aymer",
        "ivanhoe-character-john",
