      "id": "ivanhoe-source-11-p0",
      "chapterId": "ivanhoe-section-11",
      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "An empty throne",
      "description": "Proposes Rebecca as Queen to provoke the Saxons, then backs down before his own followers. Objects to Rebecca and favours Rowena. Opposes the insult and proposes that the victor choose the Queen. Warns that John’s proposal imperils their political enterprise and urges the games to begin.",
      "locationMarkerId": "ivanhoe-place-ashby-lists",
      "involvedCharacterIds": [
