      "id": "ivanhoe-source-11-p17",
      "chapterId": "ivanhoe-section-11",
      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "The laws proclaimed",
      "description": "Is among the followers surrounding John’s throne while the heralds announce the day’s rules. Attends the prince at his throne after proposing that the victor choose the Queen. Has prevailed on John to take his seat and is among the followers surrounding him for the proclamation. Assumes his throne and orders the heralds to announce the tournament rules. Holds position at one end of the lists as the proclamations conclude. Holds the other end while knights gather outside the northern barrier.",
      "locationMarkerId": "ivanhoe-place-ashby-lists",
