      "id": "ivanhoe-source-12-p5",
      "chapterId": "ivanhoe-section-12",
      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "Conjectures at the throne",
      "description": "Delays the prize and is terrified by a suggestion that the victor might be Richard. Guesses the Earl of Salisbury before the fearful rumour spreads. Suggests Multon, then rejects the Richard rumour by comparing their physiques. Reports that the victor awaits John’s pleasure. Is instructed to bring the knight forward with Wyvil.",
      "locationMarkerId": "ivanhoe-place-ashby-prince-gallery",
