      "id": "ivanhoe-source-12-p45",
      "chapterId": "ivanhoe-section-12",
      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "The archer detained",
      "description": "Orders the men-at-arms to keep the archer from leaving. States he intends to remain to see the archers of the neighbouring forests. Urges restraint of the peasants’ insolence. Responds to John’s unpopularity by a silent shrug.",
      "locationMarkerId": "ivanhoe-place-ashby-lists",
      "involvedCharacterIds": [
        "ivanhoe-character-john",
        "ivanhoe-character-yeoman",
