      "id": "ivanhoe-source-13-p29",
      "chapterId": "ivanhoe-section-13",
      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "A father’s losses",
      "description": "Paces the borrowed room grieving the fifty zecchins John took and fearing a further loss on horse and armour. Tries to console Isaac and defends rewarding the stranger’s kindness.",
