      "id": "ivanhoe-source-13-p48",
      "chapterId": "ivanhoe-section-13",
      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "Eighty zecchins",
      "description": "Reports that the steed is returned, drinks Isaac’s wine and bargains over the price of the armour. Welcomes the prospect of payment and insists on eighty zecchins despite Gurth’s offer of seventy.",
