      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "The fief of Ivanhoe",
      "description": "Reacts to Ivanhoe’s identity and defends granting the absent knight’s fief to Front-de-Bœuf. Observes that the returning victor may reclaim his manor. States that Richard had assigned the manor before John transferred it. Supports John while disputing that Jerusalem counts as a foreign country.",
