      "chapterId": "ivanhoe-section-16",
      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "Richard’s freedom reported",
      "description": "Turns pale, takes Fitzurse and De Bracy aside and explains that Richard has obtained his freedom. Receives and reads the warning passed by John. Reads the warning and questions whether it may be forged.",
