      "updatedAt": 1793232000000,
      "id": "ivanhoe-source-17-p19",
      "chapterId": "ivanhoe-section-17",
      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "A manor held of the crown",
      "description": "Invokes Cedric’s disapproval to justify Front-de-Bœuf’s holding the manor. Objects to his son’s acceptance of land as a feudal vassal and answers the Baron’s insult. Vows that neither Cedric nor Wilfred will wrest the granted estate from him.",
      "locationMarkerId": "ivanhoe-place-ashby-castle-hall",
