      "id": "ivanhoe-source-17-p33",
      "chapterId": "ivanhoe-section-17",
      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "A fragile courtesy",
      "description": "Intervenes to stop the insults and asks John to reassure Cedric. Offers conciliatory toasts to Cedric and Athelstane before asking Cedric to name a worthy Norman. Receives the toast without forgetting the insult. Drains his goblet in response to his own toast.",
      "locationMarkerId": "ivanhoe-place-ashby-castle-hall",
      "involvedCharacterIds": [
        "ivanhoe-character-fitzurse",
        "ivanhoe-character-john",
