      "updatedAt": 1793232000000,
      "id": "ivanhoe-source-17-p38",
      "chapterId": "ivanhoe-section-17",
      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "Richard’s health",
      "description": "Whispers that Cedric should name John to close the breach. Instead toasts Richard the Lion-hearted and challenges any man to reject that honour. Raises his cup mechanically, then lowers it to watch the company. Leaves his cup untouched at the toast. Also refuses the drink without openly contradicting the reigning king’s health.",
      "locationMarkerId": "ivanhoe-place-ashby-castle-hall",
      "involvedCharacterIds": [
        "ivanhoe-character-fitzurse",
