      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "A dispersing company",
      "description": "Complains that the Saxons have won the encounter and fears his adherents will desert. Announces the need to ride several miles on his homeward journey. Jests at the Prior’s hurry. Requests a private word with Aymer to secure his support at York.",
