      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "Pease and a corner",
      "description": "Are praised by the visitor as powerful guards while the hermit says the keeper lends them for his protection. Examines the spare furnishings and asks where to stable, eat and sleep. Refreshes the fire, assigns corners for horse and rider and offers parched pease.",
      "locationMarkerId": "ivanhoe-place-copmanhurst-hut",
