      "id": "ivanhoe-source-21-p12",
      "chapterId": "ivanhoe-section-21",
      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "The halter",
      "description": "Returns from the banquet, sees Gurth and orders him bound before the party rides. Submits to a halter while reproaching Cedric for caring less for his own flesh and blood. Is ordered to secure the fugitive servant. Is addressed in Cedric’s order under the source spelling Hundibert. Urges haste to preserve the expected late supper.",
