      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "A howling omen",
      "description": "Howls and bounds at the departing party, having tracked Gurth to the convent. Treats the dog as an ill omen and proposes returning until after another meal. Shares the foreboding at the gate. Recognises Gurth’s dog and insists on continuing.",
