      "id": "ivanhoe-source-22-p4",
      "chapterId": "ivanhoe-section-22",
      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "A stranded litter",
      "description": "Explains that his hired guards fled with the litter animals after hearing of outlaws. Waits beside the grounded litter. Offers two attendants and horses for a retreat to the next village. Refuses aid in anger over the earlier gallery dispute.",
