      "id": "ivanhoe-source-22-p8",
      "chapterId": "ivanhoe-section-22",
      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "Rebecca’s appeal",
      "description": "Kneels to Rowena, invokes the unnamed patient’s importance and begs protection. Persuades Cedric to use two sumpter mules for the litter and offers Rebecca a place beside her. Agrees to rearrange the baggage and include the travellers. Insists the strangers keep to the rear. Answers the insult by saying his brawn shield was left at the tournament.",
      "locationMarkerId": "ivanhoe-place-forest-litter-halt",
