      "id": "ivanhoe-source-23-p61",
      "chapterId": "ivanhoe-section-23",
      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "The key beneath the threshold",
      "description": "Leaves armed as a yeoman, locks the hut, hides the key under the threshold and refreshes himself at the fountain. Jests about the friar’s deep drink of water. Checks whether the friar is fit for service. Leaves the hut with the party after overhearing the agreement to rescue Cedric and Rowena. Goes out with the rescuers whose help he has just accepted for his master and Rowena.",
      "locationMarkerId": "ivanhoe-place-copmanhurst-fountain",
      "involvedCharacterIds": [
