      "id": "ivanhoe-source-23-p68",
      "chapterId": "ivanhoe-section-23",
      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "Called to the muster",
      "description": "Twirls his partisan, boasts of fighting the abductors and distinguishes his green cassock from his clerical frock. Orders the priest to be silent and calls the companions onward so their forces can be collected. Asks whether Front-de-Bœuf has stopped the king’s subjects on the highway. Is among the companions Locksley calls onward while demanding silence from the priest. Remains with the party outside as Locksley insists that their small rescue force must be collected.",
      "locationMarkerId": "ivanhoe-place-copmanhurst-fountain",
