      "id": "ivanhoe-source-28-p50",
      "chapterId": "ivanhoe-section-28",
      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "The knight translates",
      "description": "Reads and translates the French threat into Saxon. Is appalled by the announced intention to execute Cedric. Vows to take the castle even without siege machinery. Calls the threat a device to gain time.",
