      "id": "ivanhoe-source-28-p60",
      "chapterId": "ivanhoe-section-28",
      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "Wamba takes the frock",
      "description": "Recalls his interrupted friar’s training, volunteers, puts on the hermit’s frock and departs in disguise. Vouches for Wamba’s resourcefulness. Commissions the disguised jester to bring an account of the castle. Promises a close blockade and a severe answer to violence against the prisoners.",
