      "id": "ivanhoe-source-30-p101",
      "chapterId": "ivanhoe-section-30",
      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "The Prior’s messenger",
      "description": "Is led away with Athelstane and calls Ambrose the real Deus vobiscum as their paths cross. Is removed from the armoury among the Saxon prisoners as Ambrose is brought before the knights. Arrives distressed and reports Aymer’s capture, lost gold and ransom request. Asks directly whether the Prior has been taken. Rejects paying or mounting a rescue while his own castle is besieged. Mocks the claim that this is a safe Christian refuge.",
      "locationMarkerId": "ivanhoe-place-torquilstone-armoury",
      "involvedCharacterIds": [
