      "chapterId": "ivanhoe-section-31",
      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "An onward patient",
      "description": "Reports that the bleeding has not produced feared fever and argues he can travel next day with her care. Agrees to the York journey, persuaded by preserving the balsam’s secret and gaining Richard’s favourite as protector. Remains unconscious while the treatment and onward plan are discussed.",
