      "id": "ivanhoe-source-31-p25",
      "chapterId": "ivanhoe-section-31",
      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "Eight days of patience",
      "description": "Names Isaac as her father, notes the changed reserve and offers recovery within eight days if instructions are followed. Grows reserved on learning she is Jewish, objects to the York journey, then accepts her care and asks how to repay it.",
