      "id": "ivanhoe-source-31-p56",
      "chapterId": "ivanhoe-section-31",
      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "The hurried journey",
      "description": "Pushes a rapid pace and quarrels with hired guards about halts and food. Protects the wounded man’s travelling comfort as far as she can. Travels in the litter without the feared setback.",
      "locationMarkerId": "ivanhoe-place-isaac-northbound-road",
