      "id": "ivanhoe-source-31-p58",
      "chapterId": "ivanhoe-section-31",
      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "The name in the litter",
      "description": "Gives his name believing his captors are Saxon outlaws. Looks into the litter, discovers the wounded rival and refrains from harming him.",
