      "id": "ivanhoe-source-33-p31",
      "chapterId": "ivanhoe-section-33",
      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "Ulrica before him",
      "description": "Steps before the bed, names herself and exults in the dying power of her family’s oppressor. Calls unsuccessfully for servants to seize her and wishes to die in the fighting.",
