      "id": "ivanhoe-source-35-p17",
      "chapterId": "ivanhoe-section-35",
      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "A freeman named",
      "description": "Embraces Wamba, then pardons and frees Gurth, granting land at Walbrugham. Asks Gurth’s pardon rather than a reward for himself. Kneels, receives freedom and springs up rejoicing, calling for a smith to remove his collar. Jumps up to greet his rejoicing master.",
