      "chapterId": "ivanhoe-section-35",
      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "The returned buffet",
      "description": "Strikes the helmeted knight without moving him, then falls under the barehanded return and rises in good humour. Takes the blow, removes his gauntlet and delivers the return. Jests that the friar’s confidence in the conversion has diminished.",
