      "chapterId": "ivanhoe-section-36",
      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "A horn cannot ransom",
      "description": "Puts a frock over his green cassock and tells the Prior to make friends with money. Attempts an appeal to shared woodcraft and blows a horn. Criticises the French flourishes and adds to the demand.",
