      "chapterId": "ivanhoe-section-36",
      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "Six hundred for Aymer",
      "description": "Adopts the plan of letting each prisoner assess the other. Values the wealthy abbey’s resources and offers to advance six hundred crowns against a receipt. Protests the assessment and proposes hostages to obtain funds.",
