      "id": "ivanhoe-source-36-p39",
      "chapterId": "ivanhoe-section-36",
      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "Isaac’s assessment",
      "description": "Names a thousand crowns as Isaac’s ransom. Defends his lending, grieves Rebecca’s absence and fears she is lost. Accepts the initial assessment but hears the father’s distress.",
