      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "The Prior’s acquittance",
      "description": "Writes a six-hundred-crown receipt and obtains freedom for himself, attendants and mounts. Accepts Isaac as paymaster but refuses restoration of luxury jewels. Says he will wear the retained ornaments.",
