      "chapterId": "ivanhoe-section-37",
      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "News spoken low",
      "description": "Says he has seen Richard, was his prisoner and left him among outlaws ignorant of his identity. Turns pale and supports himself against a bench on hearing Richard is in England. Questions the report until De Bracy repeats Richard’s full name.",
