      "createdAt": 1793232000000,
      "updatedAt": 1793232000000,
      "id": "ivanhoe-source-46-p45",
      "chapterId": "ivanhoe-section-46",
      "timelineId": "ivanhoe-reading-order",
      "title": "Time allowed",
      "description": "Maintains her innocence and asks for the permitted delay. Turns his horse and reaches Rebecca’s chair as the herald does. Carries the question and answer between prisoner and Grand Master, then returns to Rebecca with the granted delay. Grants a delay until the shadows fall eastward while remaining at the eastern tribunal. Questions whether Brian may approach Rebecca and hears the Master permit their communication.",
      "locationMarkerId": "ivanhoe-place-templestowe-west-lists",
      "involvedCharacterIds": [
